## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. ❌ **Using dashes in Python folder names** (use underscores: `amulet_ai_service` NOT `amulet-ai-service`)
2. ❌ Using relative imports in Python backend
3. ❌ Using Python 3.13 (compatibility issues)
4. ❌ Not handling database sessions properly
5. ❌ Using 'use client' unnecessarily in Next.js
6. ❌ Not validating user inputs
7. ❌ Exposing sensitive data in error messages
8. ❌ Not testing code before committing
9. ❌ Creating classes when functions suffice
10. ❌ Not handling async operations properly
11. ❌ Ignoring TypeScript errors
12. ❌ **Changing SeaweedFS configuration without testing** (CRITICAL)
13. ❌ **Raising exceptions during storage initialization** (causes API crash)
14. ❌ **Using `-ip` flag instead of `-ip.bind` for SeaweedFS S3** (won't start)
15. ❌ **Not waiting for SeaweedFS cluster to initialize** (30-45 seconds)
16. ❌ **Modifying working code without understanding dependencies**
17. ❌ **Editing files in wrong folder** (verify you're in `amulet_ai_service/` not `amulet-ai-service/`)

